      "title": "Upload name interpolated into a shell command",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name from the upload form into a command string. subprocess.run then executes that string through a shell. An uploader can choose a file name with shell metacharacters such as a semicolon. The server then runs that uploader's commands. Pass an argument list without shell=True. Also reject upload names that contain path separators or start with a dash.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name from the upload form into a command string. subprocess.run then executes that string through a shell.",
